 "definition": "Derive the native Cauchy limit that lets the unchanged 1e-8 endpoint envelope hold (completion revision, SU2).\n\nSU2 8.5.0 stops a coefficient field when C_cauchy < CONV_CAUCHY_EPS, where C_cauchy is the mean over\nCONV_CAUCHY_ELEMS = 100 iterations of |dC| / max(|C|, 0.1) (SU2_CFD/src/output/COutput.cpp:954-965). The acceptance\nenvelope of a functional f (work/completion/su2/pressure_loads.py::endpoint_envelope) is unchanged:\n    span + drift + two printed quanta <= 1e-8\nover the last two 100-sample windows. It is evaluated on CFx, CFz, CMy and CD.\n\n**Bound.** Let the recent window change f by S in total and the older window by at most g * S. Then\nspan <= g * S and drift <= (1 + g) * S, so\n    envelope <= (1 + 2 g) S + 2 q.\n- A monitored field f (CD, CL, CMy) at the native stop has S <= 100 * eps * max(|f|, 0.1).\n- The body-axis forces combine them: |dCFx| <= |dCD| cos a + |dCL| sin a and |dCFz| <= |dCL| cos a + |dCD| sin a.\n\nSo the envelope can hold only if\n    eps <= (1e-8 - 2 q_f) / ((1 + 2 g_f) * 100 * M_f)\nfor every functional f and every grid/angle point of the comparison. M_f is its monitored-magnitude combination,\nq_f its printed quantum, and g_f its measured older/recent change ratio over the last 200 rows of the completion\nhistories (`work/completion/su2/runs/attempt-01`, the same discretization and stops).\n\nThe result records each bound and the largest power of ten not above the smallest bound. It also records whether\nthe template value 1E-10 and the chosen 1E-11 are admissible. No native process is run.",
